  body: "# Part-week payment: scope distinction\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation; unreviewed.
    No entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured guidance distinguishes its specific
    part-week payment category from other payments covering less than a full week and links the category
    to named benefit-to-Guarantee-Credit transitions.\n\n## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 79100–79101, PDF
    page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e1035298c6c9802f7ed9e0/dmg-Chap-79.pdf#page=8)
    supports this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `0098a2267cb9b321cae6bf25b3493b3674c4e8cb1b859fcd6b8ae7d459323be8`.\n\
    \nDo not generalise an isolated transition rule to every short payment. Regulation 13A, exceptions
    and later changes require specialist review.\n\nThe capture date, the publication page's update date
    and a date stated in the guidance have different meanings. Linked legislation and memos need their
    own provision, version and applicability review.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/part-week-payments
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The two paragraphs explicitly distinguish the category and describe its Guarantee
      Credit transition scope; similarity of duration does not make all short payments the same
      category.
    evidence:
    - page: page/79/0008
      quote: "79100 This section gives guidance on how to calculate part-week payments 1 in SPC claims.
        The term\n“part-week” payment has a specific meaning in SPC. Part-week payments must not be confused
        with\n\npayments of SPC which may be made for less than a full week 2 in other circumstances.
        Guidance on\npart-week payments is at DMG 79101 et seq. Guidance on payments of SPC for periods
        of less than a full\nweek in other circumstances is at DMG 79106 et seq.\n\n\n               \
        \                       1 SPC Act 02, Sch 1, para 13; 2 SS CS (D&A) Regs, Sch 3B, para 4(b)\n\n\
        \n\n\nWhen part-week payments are appropriate\n\n79101 In SPC, part-week payments can only be
        made where existing IS, ESA(IR), JSA(IB) or UC claimants\n\nbecome entitled to the GC1. Part-week
        payments should not be made in any other circumstances.\n\n\n                                \
        \                                                    1 SPC Regs, reg 13A"
      locator: DMG 79100–79101
  - target: term/guarantee-credit
